1. Purpose

This file contains the research questions governing:

1. theory derivation and validation; and
2. the three-round, multi-model LLM Delphi study.

These questions define how evidence is coded, how LLMs may participate, how consensus is measured, how dissent is preserved, how model errors are recorded, and how independently controlled replication is evaluated.

⸻

Part III — Web4 Methodology

RQ26 — Appropriate Research Method

Research Question

What research method is most appropriate for deriving Web4 from mixed documentary, qualitative, digital, and AI-generated evidence?

Short Title

Method for Deriving Web4

Purpose

This question determines which methodological combination can support theory development without collapsing observation, interpretation, governance design, and model output into one category.

Candidate Methods

* documentary analysis;
* qualitative coding;
* digital ethnography;
* repository analysis;
* comparative case study;
* design science;
* modified Delphi review;
* systems thinking;
* and longitudinal analysis.

Working Position

No single method is sufficient. A mixed-methods and version-controlled design is required.

