Canonical Principle

The Delphi study is not designed to prove that language models are experts.

It is designed to test whether independently controlled models can:

* identify common governance needs;
* expose missing controls;
* refine architecture;
* reveal disagreement;
* generate errors;
* and help produce a more transparent research baseline.

Its validity depends on preserving independence, provenance, dissent, correction, and the limits of model authority.